cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or these outputs, please cite the paper below."
title: "Analysis pipeline and calibrated simulation for 'Keeping Agentic Traffic Under Control Where Aggressive Blocking Fails'"
abstract: >-
  Analysis pipeline and calibrated simulation behind a four-year study of how
  automated agents respond to real production friction: difference-in-differences
  event studies over 6.05 billion requests and 49,080 labelled agents from the
  AGWA corpus, observability-collapse, lead-lag, dose-selection and
  identity-rotation robustness batteries, and the containment-threshold policy
  simulation.
